  "definitions": {
    "tokens": "Summed over the API requests recorded in the session transcripts of the coordinator and its subagents; each request counts once. Requests Claude Code makes for itself, such as context compaction, permission checks and page summaries, are not recorded there and are not included.",
    "input_uncached": "Input tokens neither read from nor written to the prompt cache.",
    "cache_write_5m": "Input tokens written to the prompt cache with a 5-minute lifetime. Cache writes in transcripts that don't give the lifetime (older Claude Code versions) are counted here.",
    "cache_write_1h": "Input tokens written to the prompt cache with a 1-hour lifetime.",
    "cache_read": "Input tokens read from the prompt cache.",
    "output": "Output tokens, including reasoning tokens.",
    "active_hours": "Wall-clock hours during which at least one of the agents counted was waiting on a model response or running a tool; agents working in parallel count once. Left out: the time after an agent ended its turn, handed back or hit a usage limit, until its next message; waiting for the user; and any gap over 10 minutes between consecutive entries of one agent's transcript, such as a suspended computer. Shorter pauses are counted.",
    "phase": "The pass a subagent ran: section (section passes), credit map (companion credit map), consolidation, draft (drafting and redrafting findings), persona check (author-persona checks), apply (applying their verdicts), publish (publishing steps such as the JSON), or other. A helper launched by a subagent counts in its parent's phase. The coordinator's own requests, across all passes, are the phase coordinator.",
    "by_agent": "One row per subagent, in launch order, labelled by the description it was launched with; a helper launched by a subagent is labelled after its parent. A resumed subagent's later work stays in its row. finding is the slug, in precedence-findings.json, of the one finding the label names, or null.",
    "procedure_deviations": "True when the run departed from the skill's procedure in a way that could change its cost or its findings.",
    "deviation_extra_tokens": "The coordinator's estimate, by kind, of the tokens that the deviations added, such as work redone, relaunched or run as a test: the agents it names, or the share of an agent's work it judged extra, plus any estimate it made otherwise. includes_unknown is true when part of the effect could not be estimated and is left out.",
    "deviation_saved_tokens": "The coordinator's estimate, by kind, of the tokens that the deviations saved, such as steps skipped or shortened, or work taken from an earlier run: multiples of comparable agents of this run, plus any estimate it made otherwise. includes_unknown as above."
  },
